so I Claire Hughes being the properly  appointed acting returning officer for  the UK parliamentary election for the  Forest of Dean constituency on the 7th  of may 2015 do hereby declare that the  number of votes cast for each candidate  at this election is as follows Chris  Coleman 2630 James Greenwood 2703 mark  harper 23 thousand 191 Steve Perry home  12,000 204 and Steve Stanberry 8790 to  know ballot papers were rejected for 12  the fish'll mark 64 were rejected for  voting for more than one candidate three  were rejected by writing or mark by  which the voter could be identified and  117 were rejected for unmarked or void  for uncertainty and there was a total  number of votes cast a 49 phase and 704  congratulations mark  um ladies and gentlemen I'll be as brief  as I can given I know you've all been  working extremely hard first of all I'd  like to thank the returning officer and  her staff I know having walked around  the room how long you've been here and  and how how much efforts been gone into  this and I think you probably want to go  to bed and I'd also thank the police for  the work that they've done I'd also like  to thank my campaign team those that  have worked over the years those that  work for me my parliamentary office and  those that worked incredibly hard  through this campaign and at this count  I would also like to thank the other  candidates and I want to say something  that's not always very popular but I  think anyone who stands for elected  office who's prepared to put themselves  out there and subject themselves to the  electorate deserves credit and I don't  think it's helpful if politicians join  in the denigration that we sometimes get  those of us in public life from the  media and others not everyone is  prepared to put themselves forward to  give the electorate a choice so I thank  all those that made this a contest but  most of all I'd like to thank that the  people of the forest of dean for once  again putting their trust in me to be  there member of parliament for the  forthcoming Parliament I'm very pleased  with the campaign that we ran here in  the forest of dean I think it was a very  positive campaign focused on the issues  and not on the other candidates I think  we run a very positive campaign  nationally the very clear issue that  came through for me on the doorstep was  I think the public do want us to finish  the job we started five years ago about  putting the economy right we haven't  seen all the results from across the  country but I am hopeful that in the  next few hours the Prime Minister will  be able to continue  work over the next parliament and I look  forward to working with him in whatever  capacity he determines to put the people  of the forest of dean first and to do  what I can to serve them and to serve  our country thank you very much indeed
 

